ENTRY            C3126   20260422   20260819   20260819       C258
SUBENT        C3126001   20260422   20260819   20260819       C258
BIB                  8         26
TITLE      Low-energy measurement of the 25Mg(alpha,n)28Si
           reaction via neutron spectroscopy
AUTHOR     (Shahina,K.T.Macon,A.Boeltzig,R.J.deBoer,M.Febbraro,
           S.Aguilar,T.Anderson,U.Bajpai,S.P.Burcher,Y.Chen,
           A.Clark,A.Dombos,C.Dulal,B.Frentz,O.Gomez,J.Gorres,
           A.Gula,S.L.Henderson,K.Howard,K.L.Jones,J.Kelly,
           R.Kelmar,J.M.Kovoor,Q.Liu,A.Majumdar,K.Manukyan,
           L.Morales,S.Mosby,S.Moylan,A.Nelson,S.D.Pain,
           P.Scholz,C.Reingold,M.Renaud,N.Sensharma,C.Seymour,
           G.Seymour,E.Stech,W.Tan,R.Toomey,B.Vande Kolk,
           J.Wilkinson,M.Wiescher)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,113,035802,2026)
           #doi:10.1103/rzb1-t6bt
INSTITUTE  (1USAMIT,1USANOT,2GERZFK,1USAORL,1USAAFT,1USATEN,
           1USALAS,1USAANL,1USARUT)
FACILITY   (VDG,1USANOT) A 5 MV Pelletron accelerator at the
           University of Notre Dame Nuclear Science Laboratory.
SAMPLE     (12-MG-25,ENR=0.99) The target was fabricated by
           evaporating isotopically enriched 25Mg (99%) metal
           onto a thin Ta backing of 0.5 mm thickness. 25Mg
           target thicknesses of 78(8) microg/cm2 and 33(3)
           microg/cm2 for the thick and thin targets,
           respectively. Note that in the close geometry setup
           the effective target thickness is 110(11) microg/cm2.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by R.J.deBoer on April 24, 2026.
HISTORY    (20260422C) BP
ENDBIB              26
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           29
SUBENT        C3126002   20260422   20260819   20260819       C258
BIB                  6         20
REACTION   (12-MG-25(A,N)14-SI-28,PAR,DA)
DETECTOR   (SCIN) The deuterated liquid scintillator (EJ-315M)
           was from the ODeSA array.
METHOD     Neutron detection using a deuterated liquid
           scintillator from the ODeSA array.
ANALYSIS   The experimental spectra have been analyzed by
           applying spectrum unfolding techniques to improved
           background discrimination for the 25Mg(alpha,n)28Si
           reaction at low energies, down to Ealpha=1.75 MeV.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainties.
           (ERR-S,1.,50.) Statistical uncertainties.
           (ERR-SYS) Total systematic.
           (ERR-1) Beam alignment.
           (ERR-2) Target stability/homogeneity.
           (ERR-3) Spectrum unfolding.
           (ERR-4) Current reading.
           (ERR-5) Target thickness.
           (ERR-6) Efficiency.
STATUS     (TABLE,,Shahina+,J,PR/C,113,035802,2026) Supplemental
           Material
ENDBIB              20
COMMON               8          6
E-LVL      ERR-SYS    ERR-1      ERR-2      ERR-3      ERR-4
ERR-5      ERR-6
